From: kusti420 <virtuaalnepannkook@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3-msm: don't log the DBM update-transfer lookup for non-DBM endpoints

dwc3_stop_active_transfer() notifies DWC3_CONTROLLER_NOTIFY_DISABLE_UPDXFER on
every End Transfer, and dwc3_msm_dbm_disable_updxfer() logs its entry and,
through find_matching_dbm_ep(), "No DBM EP matches USB EP n" for any endpoint
that is not a DBM endpoint. The stock Samsung dwc3-msm.c maps dev_dbg to
dev_err ("#undef dev_dbg / #define dev_dbg dev_err"), so both lines reach the
kernel log at error level.

The isochronous UVC streaming endpoint ends its transfer after every frame
(dwc3 stops an isochronous transfer once its request list is empty), so
"Use phone as webcam" logged 2 lines per frame, about 54 per second at 30 fps
(3377 pairs in a 3-mode, 60 s per mode capture), pushing everything else out
of the ring buffer.

Look the endpoint up without logging in dwc3_msm_dbm_disable_updxfer() and log
the entry only for DBM endpoints. DBM endpoints behave exactly as before
(same lookup, same register write); for other endpoints the function still
returns -ENODEV, which the notifier ignores, as before. find_matching_dbm_ep()
and its other callers (DBM endpoint configuration) are unchanged.

Used by MonsterROM target/a52sxq/patches/usb_webcam.
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c
index 8fe793df8..cadc40bbf 100755
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c
@@ -831,11 +831,19 @@ static int dwc3_msm_dbm_disable_updxfer(struct dwc3 *dwc, u8 usb_ep)
 	u32 data;
 	int dbm_ep;
 
-	dev_dbg(mdwc->dev, "%s\n", __func__);
+	/*
+	 * Called for every End Transfer (dwc3_stop_active_transfer()), e.g.
+	 * once per frame on the isochronous UVC endpoint. Only DBM endpoints
+	 * have an update-transfer bit to disable: look the endpoint up quietly
+	 * (dev_dbg is dev_err in this file) and log only for DBM endpoints.
+	 */
+	for (dbm_ep = 0; dbm_ep < mdwc->dbm_num_eps; dbm_ep++)
+		if (mdwc->dbm_ep_num_mapping[dbm_ep] == usb_ep)
+			break;
+	if (dbm_ep == mdwc->dbm_num_eps)
+		return -ENODEV;
 
-	dbm_ep = find_matching_dbm_ep(mdwc, usb_ep);
-	if (dbm_ep < 0)
-		return dbm_ep;
+	dev_dbg(mdwc->dev, "%s\n", __func__);
 
 	data = msm_dbm_read_reg(mdwc, DBM_DISABLE_UPDXFER);
 	data |= (0x1 << dbm_ep);
